# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your TypeSafe API key after the `=`.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Get a key at https://typesafe.ai (Jev is in early access — join the waitlist there).
# Leave it empty (or don't create .env.local at all) to run in demo mode with simulated results.
# The key is only ever read on the server; it is never sent to the browser.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
#
# Or keep no key on disk at all. Store it in 1Password and run:
#
#   pnpm dev:1password
#
# That reads the key at launch and passes it to the dev server in memory. An
# already-set environment variable beats .env.local in Next's loader, so it works
# whether or not you also have a plaintext key above. It defaults to the item
# `op://Development/Jev API Key/password`; override with TYPESAFE_OP_REF.
